WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.440
<b>Four Years Ago</b>

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.440
You did that all for your little sibs?

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:14.150
Swear you'll turn over a new leaf, 
and I'll pretend this never happened.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.930
Keep gambling to a hobby, okay?

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.630
<i>In response to an increase in heinous crimes,</i>

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:33.090
<i>a new movement is picking up steam in police 
and security forces around the world.</i>

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:39.080
<i>This is the story of the services 
performed by ACTIVE in Japan.</i>

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:52.630
<b>File 5: Poker Face of Erasure</b>

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.350
Oh? Logos?

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.510
Some say their existence is 
just an Internet rumor.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:13.230
<b>Every Day Is a Good Day</b>

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.060
Let's cut to the chase.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:08.150
We believe the criminal organization 
known as Logos exists.

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:11.920
And why would the star of public 
safety share that with us?

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:13.230
And under the table, at that.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:18.910
I saw in a report that several 
incidents you handled

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.460
may have involved Logos. That's why.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.610
I thought I should inform you, just in case.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:30.250
I thought our opinions were prone to be ignored.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:35.460
It's true that some don't approve of an 
experimental department voicing opinions.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.120
Now, now...

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.830
So, Hayashida-san,

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:43.460
what's Logos after? Money, as usual?

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.040
We don't know yet.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:47.300
This is only a hunch,

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.600
but it could be just to stir up mischief.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.810
Mischief, eh?

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:56.070
Are the bigwigs done yet?

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.540
Uh, who're you?

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.250
So you're Kuroki-kun?

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:00.900
I'll take my leave now.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:08.870
<b>Every Day Is a Good Day</b>

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:05.960
If you're done talking work, 
we need you two back there.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:07.590
Everyone's waiting.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:08.870
Yes, yes.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:21.380
<b>Kikyou</b>

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:12.900
Sorry we're late!

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:13.870
We've been waiting.

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:14.730
How did the work talk go?

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.570
Oh, it went, I guess.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.130
How may I help you?

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.380
I'd like another of this pomegranate cocktail 
said to be good for female hormones!

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:23.760
<i>Hormones?</i>

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.320
<i>She honestly needs more?</i>

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.640
I'll also have more hormo—

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.490
I mean, pomegranate juice.

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:32.030
Also, a pitcher of beer.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.350
Okay, cheers!

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:35.720
You're moving way too fast.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:36.570
<b>Kikyou</b>

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:41.180
So you're really paying this time,
Kuroki-kun? What brought this on?

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.490
It's apparently to celebrate his casino win.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.530
Casino?

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.200
The one in Special District Numazu.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:49.330
I wish you guys could've seen my valiant self!

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.220
Well, that's impressive.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:54.060
All hail the passing of the casino bill!

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:57.790
Actually, there was a gambler who made 
headlines a few years ago, wasn't there?

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:00.940
Bloody Mary?

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:04.330
She was called the Empress of 
Illegal Casinos, wasn't she?

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.800
I stopped hearing about her after
the bill was passed, though.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:10.200
So she was never caught?

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.770
That's how it came to pass 
that I joined this division.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:14.800
Huh?

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.160
K-Kuroki...

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:19.390
You're acting proud, but what was 
your total windfall, anyway?

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:21.190
About 200,000 in the red, I guess.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:22.000
Huh?

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:26.280
Pomegranate cocktail, pomegranate juice, 
and a pitcher of beer.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.240
Oh, where are Kyoukai-san and Madoka-san?

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.850
I invited them, but Kyoukai-san's working late.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:34.460
Madoka just ignored me.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.560
Ignored?

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:42.090
<b>Metropolitan Government Building Exit, 
Nihon-Oodoori Station, Yokohama</b>

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:43.830
Target disembarked from the Minatomirai 
Line at Nihon-Oodoori Station at 19:27h,

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:45.600
then took the Metropolitan 
Government Building exit.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:47.470
Target appears headed toward the harbor.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.620
Why am I doing this?

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.740
Madoka-chan doesn't ignore people.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:56.350
Maybe she just answered you really quietly?

00:04:56.610 --> 00:05:00.190
Then I wonder if it's just like 
what the Ogikubo guys said.

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:03.370
What's this about?

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.790
Madoka-chan can be a little mysterious,

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:09.270
so the Ogikubo Branch was saying

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:12.650
that she might be a spy from Logos

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:15.360
or some other type of government agency.

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:17.170
Of course it's just a joke, though.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.900
We're an odd bunch,

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:24.760
so Madoka could be a spy with Internal Affairs.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.880
A s-spy with Internal Affairs?

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.460
All right, let's look into this.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.710
I suppose we have no choice.

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:33.920
Asami-chan...

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.210
We're counting on you.

00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:37.210
Huh?

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:42.160
19:50h. Target is walking in Yamashita Park.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:44.650
No irregular behavior observed.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:47.950
<b>Game Center</b>

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.070
20:35h.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:50.380
Target is playing a UFO 
catcher game at the arcade

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:53.080
near Chinatown's east gate in 
Naka Ward, Yokohama City.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:56.460
Target acquires a stuffed animal of 
a presumably minor character.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:05:59.960
21:22h.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:03.940
Target enters Nyan Ma La, 
a Chinese restaurant in the area.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:09.220
<b>Extra Spicy Chinese Restaurant  
Nyan Ma La</b>

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.220
"Extra Spicy"?

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.080
Deducing entry into the 
restaurant to be dangerous.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:13.430
Standing by outside.

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.100
Liver-leek stir-fry.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:20.810
Coming right up.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:25.530
That's odd...

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.320
It's already been over 
two hours since she went in.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:30.620
Welcome.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:33.160
Um, I'm meeting someone here.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:38.730
She's gone?

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:39.580
That's impossible.

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:42.500
What?

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:54.600
To prevent miniaturized 
missiles from being fired...

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:56.490
Play in a casino poker match?

00:06:56.490 --> 00:07:00.630
Yes. According to Tokyo Prefecture, 
that's the perp's demand.

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:03.300
The specifics are rather strange.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:08.380
There's a math instructor named Onodera 
Ryou at Kichijouji's Touzai Cram School.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:11.620
We're to play and win against him.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.820
Anyone can play him at once, no matter how many.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:15.360
But why us?

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:18.250
There must be others who are good at poker.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.630
You know about the explosion 
in Yamashita-chou last night?

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:23.290
Oh, you mean...

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.190
Yeah.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:27.090
Five poker experts have already been defeated.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:31.960
So they're saying to do whatever 
it takes to win, even cheating?

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:33.900
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.680
It's not that you're fraudsters.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.770
You just have more leeway in 
equipment and the division...

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:39.980
Okay!

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:41.980
That'll be the official line.

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:43.450
And that's the deal.

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:45.860
Even if it's Inagi-san asking,

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:50.320
why not just cut right to it, and destroy 
all missiles within the prefecture?

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:52.250
That would be difficult.

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:53.030
Huh?

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:57.990
The missiles have a shield-machine function.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:00.200
They're typically buried underground.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:02.730
They aren't particularly strong,

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:05.420
but it's near impossible to 
find them before launch.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.090
I see. Then I'll do it!

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:09.620
I can do poker!

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:10.800
Yeah, denied.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:11.930
Huh?

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:13.590
Where's Madoka-chan, by the way?

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:15.010
She's off duty...

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:18.830
Oh, did you know Asami-chan actually tailed her?

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:19.400
Huh?

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:20.970
But you said to do it.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:23.190
It was just a joke at a drinking party.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.360
What?!

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.400
I went all the way to Yokohama!

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:30.290
We can review that incident at a later time.

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:32.360
I'll play the poker game.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:33.710
You, Funasaka-san?

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:35.290
Is this a joke?

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:37.320
I'm sorry I kept this from you for so long.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.410
I may not look it,

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:43.290
but in my younger days, I nearly destroyed 
myself with drink, women, and gambling.

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:44.460
Huh...

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:47.560
Uh, but still...

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:50.170
If you almost destroyed yourself, 
doesn't that mean you're bad at it?

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:51.600
Hmm...

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:55.500
Okay. I'll let Funasaka-san handle this.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.440
Leek-liver stir-fry.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.440
Onodera-san, was it?

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:16.040
Oh, y-yes.

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:16.860
Nice to meet you.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:20.090
N-Nice to meet you, as well.

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:22.340
So, who's the one

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:25.080
who keeps sending players to me?

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:28.870
<i>As I suspected, this man doesn't 
seem to know anything.</i>

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:32.510
How may I help you?

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:33.780
Vodka martini.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.470
Shaken, not stirred.

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:38.430
Certainly, sir.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:41.140
Sh-She's got the whole act down.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:44.850
It just might turn out to be a square match.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:57.320
Check.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:59.780
O-Okay. 200.

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:00.740
Call.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:10.080
Um, I have no idea what the rules are.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.040
Kyoukai-kun...

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.890
On it.

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:15.660
I sent the rule data over.

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:17.800
Th-Thank you.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.930
O-Okay, 500.

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:24.930
<i>Having two queens is giving him confidence.</i>

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:26.640
Call.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:29.390
1,000.

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:33.080
<i>At the least, he has a two pair, 
sevens and queens.</i>

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:36.200
<i>He could have a full house, but...</i>

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:38.530
Call.

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:41.170
Showdown, please.

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.790
T-Two pair, queens and sevens.

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:48.370
Three of a kind.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:49.620
I win.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:50.830
All right!

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:52.790
<b>Extra Spicy Chinese Restaurant  
Nyan Ma La</b>

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:03.090
Hello, miss.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.690
Here again?

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.950
Want to join us?

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:10.270
We won't lose today. It's time for payback.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:12.330
These days, not too many people

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:15.900
understand the true nature of gambling like you.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:17.460
Who would've thought that

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:20.490
legalizing gambling would 
change so many things?

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:24.900
Yeah, all those special arenas 
and Internet streams...

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:30.250
Even the guy who used to hunt us 
enjoys safe, legal gambling now.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.460
Hunt you?

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:36.460
Yeah, although he was a loser 
who failed in his investigation.

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:38.730
He lost again.

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:40.670
Guess he only won the first round.

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:43.550
What's wrong?

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:51.570
Guess we won't be seeing her card-handling today.

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:56.930
Yeah, her skills remind me of those 
of that legendary female gambler.

00:11:56.930 --> 00:11:59.090
She was only active for a year,

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:02.030
wore a china dress, and hid her face.

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:04.600
She must've only been a teen back then.

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:08.490
I wonder what Bloody Mary's up to these days.

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:15.710
Straight.

00:12:16.140 --> 00:12:19.130
<i>Th-This man's good at his game.</i>

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:21.770
<i>He was hesitant at first,</i>

00:12:21.770 --> 00:12:23.800
<i>but he gradually grew expressionless.</i>

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.890
<i>He might as well be wearing a death mask now.</i>

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:28.220
<i>I can't discern what he's thinking at all!</i>

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:32.270
<b>Express Suruga 

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:34.600
<i>The 20:07 train bound for Special 
District Numazu, Suruga Island...</i>

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:38.230
Onodera's out for the kill.

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:45.740
Is Funasaka-san okay?

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:49.200
Haruka-chan, commence
Operation Manchaku No. 6!

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.530
Hello!

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.340
Would you like anything to drink?

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:53.830
No, thank you.

00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:56.960
We have the data.

00:12:57.190 --> 00:13:00.290
Heart rate, breath rate, and 
perspiration levels are all elevated.

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:01.880
They're above normal values.

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:03.930
He's lying.

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:06.390
Funasaka-san, he's bluffing.

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:08.340
Call.

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:09.300
All in.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:12.140
Showdown, please.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:13.850
Three of a kind.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:16.410
Straight.

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:17.100
Huh?

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:20.220
Wh-What the...

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:21.740
Impossible.

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:24.120
I'm getting alternating normal 
and abnormal readings!

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:25.320
Could he be...

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:30.240
Your tricks are a waste of time.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:35.480
I can fool a polygraph with ease.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:38.310
I... I lost.

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:39.810
This won't do.

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:42.380
I need you to try a little longer.

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:45.670
If you don't, another missile will go flying.

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:49.300
How did he know about the missiles?

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:50.890
Wait, so he's...

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:57.290
You're the one who came up 
with this death game?!

00:13:57.290 --> 00:13:59.340
What choice did I have?

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:03.470
It's the casino's fault for blacklisting 
me out of fear due to my skills.

00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:05.280
But how did you get the missiles?!

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:08.910
I got them from people 
who call themselves "Logos."

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:10.060
Logos!

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:12.300
He didn't even bother hiding the name.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:15.200
There should be a couple more missiles.

00:14:15.690 --> 00:14:19.290
Logos is supposed to decide when to launch them.

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:22.920
But if I lose, the missiles won't be launched.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:25.550
So let's try a little longer.

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:29.340
You can try any trick you have up your sleeve.

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:31.680
Then, for starters, we'll swap out players!

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.730
Sure. I don't mind.

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:39.100
Oh, and there's someone here 
who wants to speak with you.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:42.060
Switch on. File number fox trot.

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:46.480
Well, well...

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:47.840
Wh-Who's that?

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:49.450
Onodera's mother.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.590
I'm surprised you managed a connection with her.

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:52.850
It's fake.

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:56.500
Fortunately, even her audio data was 
available on social networking sites.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:59.280
Listen to me, Ryou.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.750
<i>Listen to me, Ryou.</i>

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:05.590
<i>Please stop causing trouble!</i>

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:08.160
<i>I don't remember raising you to be this way.</i>

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:12.040
<i>Remember when you were little?</i>

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:13.970
<i>How I'd—</i>

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:14.430
Sorry.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:18.430
My mom was a drunken loser with a wandering eye.

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:22.010
She's the one who drilled me in poker, too.

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:27.900
By her command, I honed my 
skills to earn our keep.

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:29.690
Full house.

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:33.280
<i>I lost in an instant?</i>

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:36.870
I'm prepared to get caught.

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:40.540
If I have to live another dull day, 
I'd rather have one last match.

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:41.970
That'd be enough for me.

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:43.630
I've had enough.

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:47.090
Pull yourself together! 
You're just getting started!

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:48.940
It's no use! We're in trouble!

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:51.600
If I lose, a missile will be launched.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:54.600
Being 200,000 in the red is 
my personal responsibility,

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:56.300
but missile damage?!

00:15:56.630 --> 00:15:59.130
This is a rare case of accurate 
self-introspection, but...

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:01.180
Now isn't the time to be impressed by that!

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:02.270
What now?

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:05.910
No one can win against a guy like him.

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:10.190
Oh? That's all?

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:12.950
Are you sure? A city's going to go up in flames.

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:15.760
I wonder what Logos will target.

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:17.410
I can't wait to find out.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:21.570
Let's see how far the police can track Logos...

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:22.410
Hmm?

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:23.790
<b>This is boring, YO. 
Let's fire the missile! lol</b>

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:25.050
Dog...

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:29.010
Like I said, our goal isn't to hurt people.

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:30.720
What's the missile targ— Huh?

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:36.260
What? Aren't you off duty?

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:37.550
I'll play him.

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:39.010
What?!

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:41.100
You know how to play poker?

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:49.680
Oh, the livecast...

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:53.080
Wait just a moment. I'll try this circuit...

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:56.700
Oh, look. It's the girl.

00:16:56.920 --> 00:16:57.910
Straight.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:16:59.870
That's a win, right?

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:03.390
Madoka-chan won?

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:04.790
But that's just one round.

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:06.250
Flush.

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:07.710
Full house.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:08.920
Four of a kind.

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:10.550
Straight flush.

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:11.710
<i>She's his equal...</i>

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:14.570
<i>And both are equally impassive.</i>

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:17.510
<i>It's like two dead people 
playing against each other.</i>

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:20.400
Not good. She lacks her usual flair.

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:22.470
Is she too distracted by the audience?

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:23.930
Full house.

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.140
Two pair.

00:17:25.430 --> 00:17:26.350
Flush.

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:28.310
Crap! She's falling behind!

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:31.650
Asami-chan, access the dealer robot's controls.

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:34.430
We'll control the cards that are dealt.

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:36.250
I can't.

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:38.910
That robot has an anti-fraud function,

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:41.170
AKA a conscience circuit.

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:43.950
Any external tampering, and it'll freeze.

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:47.420
Damn Community Safety Division... 
No one asked for that!

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:54.710
Time out.

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:55.830
Very well.

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:57.680
Only fifteen minutes, though.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:58.900
Madoka-kun?

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.350
Sena-kun, ready the Wear.

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:02.570
Understood.

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:04.930
What's the projected missile target?

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:09.760
Fifteen minutes.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.640
I guess I win.

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:13.980
No, you lose.

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:24.210
M-Madoka-kun...

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:26.580
You... You're...

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.270
Bloody Mary.

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:31.790
You know you're about to lose 
your place in society?

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:32.960
Madoka-san's...

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.090
...the legendary...

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.300
...gambler?!

00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:39.750
I had no idea Bloody Mary was so young.

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:41.410
You have my respect.

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:43.010
That is, if you're really her.

00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:45.930
Straight.

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:47.140
Flush.

00:18:51.050 --> 00:18:52.480
Another draw?

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:55.420
No, we're moving toward a conclusion.

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:58.280
Yeah. This is a big game.

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:02.990
<b>Verifying</b>

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:03.990
<b>Approved</b>

00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:15.550
I hope our predictions are correct with 
regard to the missile launch site.

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:21.720
<i>This is it. This hand will decide it.</i>

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:24.100
<i>Could it be a straight flush?</i>

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:26.160
<i>No, the possibility of that is low.</i>

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:27.620
<i>Maybe a flush?</i>

00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:30.360
<i>If it's just a straight, I win, but...</i>

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:43.170
Why are they just staring at each other?

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:45.460
Maybe I'll heat things up.

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:48.950
Dog!

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:50.420
Thermal signature detected...

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:52.040
Crap, the missile's been launched!

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.120
What's the launch point?

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:55.450
Candidate two, Azabu Juuban.

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:58.340
<b>Haneda Airport 

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:57.290
It's flying southwest.

00:19:57.290 --> 00:19:58.340
Oscar I.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:19:59.410
I'll give it a shot.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:04.590
Twenty-five seconds until impact!

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:06.260
No, it won't be in time!

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.260
Request deactivation of sublimation function.

00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:10.320
Permission granted!

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:14.760
I see it now...

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:18.570
Your poker face has a slight flaw.

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:21.630
When you bluff, your eyes 
twitch ever so slightly.

00:20:21.630 --> 00:20:23.990
That's right, this is a bluff.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:25.410
All in!

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:26.620
Call.

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:29.450
Showdown, please.

00:20:29.730 --> 00:20:31.160
Full house.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:32.610
I win.

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:39.090
Type 21 charged-particle launcher, fire!

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:45.610
You don't deserve to gamble.

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:49.390
You're just a corpse that drowned in gambling,

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:51.620
a drifter in the darkness.

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:54.260
The true pleasure of gambling

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:58.560
is to leave it and return to the light of day.

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:02.280
Say what you will, loser.

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:03.860
Straight...

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:05.490
flush.

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:12.510
I win.

00:21:13.150 --> 00:21:14.600
Also, this...

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:16.460
was deliberate.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:24.410
I... lost?

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:28.450
The end of one game

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.970
is the beginning of another.

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:33.240
Let's meet again.

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:38.160
Um, would you like anything 
to drink, Madoka-san?

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:39.250
Pomegranate hoppy.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:41.600
Oh, for female hormones? Okay.

00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:43.640
What would you like to eat?

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:45.740
Liver-leek stir-fry... Oh.

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:46.840
Liver-leek stir-fry!

00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:48.650
We don't have anything like that.

00:21:48.650 --> 00:21:50.950
Pretty please?

00:21:51.190 --> 00:21:53.910
Um, Funasaka-san, I...

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:54.680
Hmm?

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:57.440
I really didn't recognize you until then...

00:21:57.930 --> 00:21:58.810
Um...

00:21:58.810 --> 00:22:00.230
What are you talking about?

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:03.800
You rushed over while off-duty 
to help your teammates.

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:05.140
What's so bad about that?

00:22:05.140 --> 00:22:08.090
A little cosplay won't get you arrested.

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:11.120
But if I were to say anything...

00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:11.970
Yes?

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:14.090
Moderation is key with any hobby.

00:22:14.090 --> 00:22:16.560
For your younger siblings' sakes, as well.

00:22:17.970 --> 00:22:18.640
Right!

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:51.860
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:50.840 --> 00:23:52.200
Ohakonyapachininko!

00:23:51.860 --> 00:24:04.870
File 6: Dreams Beyond the Twilight

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:53.780
I'm predicting the next episode!

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:55.460
H-Hey...

00:23:55.460 --> 00:23:57.830
A middle-aged man on a date 
with a nineteen-year-old?

00:23:57.830 --> 00:24:00.260
Will this December love end in tragedy?

00:24:00.260 --> 00:24:02.600
Next time, "Dreams Beyond the Twilight."

00:24:02.600 --> 00:24:04.090
Be sure to watch!
